From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:08:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvk: VK_NV_framebuffer_mixed_samples, rasterization at
 more samples than the color attachments

Direct2D fills anti-aliased paths (the Windows 11 shell's vector icons,
complex geometry) with D3D11.1 target-independent rasterization:
ForcedSampleCount 16 in the rasterizer state with a single-sample render
target, and a pixel shader that takes its alpha from the number of
covered samples in SV_Coverage divided by 16.  Vulkan can only express
that with mixed samples (rasterizationSamples 16, color attachment 1
sample); without it DXVK rasterizes at the attachment's single sample,
the coverage has one bit, and every covered pixel gets 1/16 of its alpha
(a Direct2D test fill: maximum alpha 16 instead of 255).

The hardware has done this since Maxwell B: SET_TIR RASTER_N_TARGET_M
with SET_ANTI_ALIAS_RASTER giving the raster sample count, next to
SET_ANTI_ALIAS for the attachments.  VK_NV_framebuffer_mixed_samples
(Maxwell B+):

- nvk_flush_mixed_samples(), when the rasterization samples or the
  coverage modulation state change (every render pass begin dirties the
  former): rasterizationSamples above the attachments' count turns
  target-independent rasterization on with that raster sample count, and
  off otherwise.  The pixel shader's covmask then has one bit per raster
  sample; without sample shading NAK hands it to gl_SampleMaskIn as is.
- CLEAR_SURFACE with target-independent rasterization on is a class
  error (GB202: Xid 69, CLEAR_SURFACE 0x19d0, error code 0x124), so it
  is turned off at every render pass begin (before SET_ANTI_ALIAS and
  the load-op clears) and before vkCmdClearAttachments; the next draw
  that wants it turns it back on.  A CPU flag (on at command buffer
  begin and after secondaries) keeps the off method to once.
- At queue init: off, coverage reduced to the color samples by the
  affinity map (the extension's merge reduction), alpha to coverage and
  the occlusion sample count on the raster samples (the spec orders
  multisample coverage and sample counting before coverage reduction).
- Coverage modulation (VkPipelineCoverageModulationStateCreateInfoNV and
  the extended dynamic state 3 coverage modulation mode, table enable and
  table, now exposed): SET_TIR_MODULATION component select, the linear
  function or the 16-entry unorm8 coefficient table.
- The standard sample positions of the raster sample count go to the
  hardware; the shader-visible copy keeps NVK_MAX_SAMPLES (8) entries, as
  sample shading is not allowed with mixed samples.

The extension requires sampleShadingEnable = VK_FALSE with mixed samples
and a depth/stencil attachment of rasterizationSamples samples when a
depth or stencil test is on, so the per-pass sample masks and the
depth/stencil layout stay as they are.  A device without the extension
enabled emits nothing new.
---
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_buffer.c      |   4 +
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_buffer.h      |  11 ++
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_clear.c       |  10 +-
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_draw.c        | 172 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c |   7 +-
 5 files changed, 196 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_buffer.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_buffer.c
index cc5c173d..05d7bf35 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_buffer.c
@@ -466,6 +466,10 @@ nvk_CmdExecuteCommands(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer,
       cmd->indirect_push_synced = false;
       cmd->state.gfx.fs_tail_dw_count = 0;
       cmd->state.gfx.draw_sysvals_emitted = 0;
+      /* The secondary may leave target-independent rasterization on */
+      cmd->state.gfx.tir_maybe_on = true;
+      BITSET_SET(cmd->vk.dynamic_graphics_state.dirty,
+                 MESA_VK_DYNAMIC_MS_RASTERIZATION_SAMPLES);
 
       if (prof_slot >= 0) {
          nvk_pass_profile_end_secondary(cmd, other, prof_slot);
diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_buffer.h b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_buffer.h
index 9869fa60..abade3c9 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_buffer.h
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_buffer.h
@@ -260,6 +260,15 @@ struct nvk_graphics_state {
     */
    uint8_t zcull_internal;
 
+   /* VK_NV_framebuffer_mixed_samples: target-independent rasterization
+    * (SET_TIR) may be on.  True at command buffer begin and after
+    * secondaries (whatever ran before may have left it on), set when a draw
+    * turns it on, cleared when it is turned off.  CLEAR_SURFACE with it on
+    * is a class error (Xid 69 on GB202), so render pass begins and
+    * vkCmdClearAttachments turn it off first.
+    */
+   bool tir_maybe_on;
+
    struct nvk_draw_params_state {
       bool valid;
       uint32_t first_vertex;
@@ -452,6 +461,8 @@ nvk_cmd_buffer_push_indirect_ext(struct nvk_cmd_buffer *cmd,
                                  uint64_t addr, uint32_t range,
                                  bool no_prefetch);
 
+void nvk_cmd_disable_tir(struct nvk_cmd_buffer *cmd);
+
 void nvk_cmd_buffer_begin_graphics(struct nvk_cmd_buffer *cmd,
                                    const VkCommandBufferBeginInfo *pBeginInfo);
 void nvk_cmd_buffer_begin_compute(struct nvk_cmd_buffer *cmd,
diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_clear.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_clear.c
index bcfe072c..4d666891 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_clear.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_clear.c
@@ -150,7 +150,15 @@ nvk_CmdClearAttachments(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer,
                         const VkClearRect *pRects)
 {
    VK_FROM_HANDLE(nvk_cmd_buffer, cmd, commandBuffer);
-   const struct vk_dynamic_graphics_state *dyn = &cmd->vk.dynamic_graphics_state;
+   struct vk_dynamic_graphics_state *dyn = &cmd->vk.dynamic_graphics_state;
+
+   /* CLEAR_SURFACE is a class error with target-independent rasterization
+    * on; the next draw turns it back on if it wants it.
+    */
+   if (cmd->state.gfx.tir_maybe_on) {
+      nvk_cmd_disable_tir(cmd);
+      BITSET_SET(dyn->dirty, MESA_VK_DYNAMIC_MS_RASTERIZATION_SAMPLES);
+   }
 
    struct nv_push *p = nvk_cmd_buffer_push(cmd, 4 + attachmentCount * 4);
 
diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_draw.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_draw.c
index 0765625a..9f439c4a 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_cmd_draw.c
@@ -616,6 +616,25 @@ nvk_push_draw_state_init(struct nvk_queue *queue, struct nv_push *p)
       P_IMMD(p, NVB197, SET_POST_PS_INITIAL_COVERAGE, true);
       P_IMMD(p, NVB197, SET_OFFSET_RENDER_TARGET_INDEX,
                         BY_VIEWPORT_INDEX_FALSE);
+
+      /* VK_NV_framebuffer_mixed_samples (see nvk_flush_mixed_samples()):
+       * rasterization at more samples than the color attachments have is
+       * the hardware's target-independent rasterization, off until a draw
+       * asks for it.  While it is on, a color sample is covered if any of
+       * the raster samples associated with it is (the extension's merge
+       * reduction), and alpha to coverage and occlusion queries work on the
+       * raster samples, which the spec orders before coverage reduction.
+       */
+      P_IMMD(p, NVB197, SET_TIR, MODE_DISABLED);
+      P_IMMD(p, NVB197, SET_TIR_CONTROL, {
+         .z_pass_pixel_count_use_raster_samples =
+            Z_PASS_PIXEL_COUNT_USE_RASTER_SAMPLES_ENABLE,
+         .alpha_to_coverage_use_raster_samples =
+            ALPHA_TO_COVERAGE_USE_RASTER_SAMPLES_ENABLE,
+         .reduce_coverage = REDUCE_COVERAGE_ENABLE,
+      });
+      P_IMMD(p, NVB197, SET_TIR_MODULATION, COMPONENT_SELECT_NO_MODULATION);
+      P_IMMD(p, NVB197, SET_TIR_MODULATION_FUNCTION, SELECT_LINEAR);
    }
 
    P_IMMD(p, NV9097, SET_WINDOW_ORIGIN, {
@@ -969,6 +988,8 @@ nvk_cmd_buffer_begin_graphics(struct nvk_cmd_buffer *cmd,
                               const VkCommandBufferBeginInfo *pBeginInfo)
 {
    const struct nvk_device *dev = nvk_cmd_buffer_device(cmd);
+
+   cmd->state.gfx.tir_maybe_on = true;
    if (cmd->vk.level == VK_COMMAND_BUFFER_LEVEL_PRIMARY) {
       struct nv_push *p = nvk_cmd_buffer_push(cmd, 9);
       P_MTHD(p, NV9097, INVALIDATE_SAMPLER_CACHE_NO_WFI);
@@ -1116,6 +1137,26 @@ nil_to_nv9097_samples_mode(enum nil_sample_layout sample_layout)
 
 static uint32_t nvk_mme_anti_alias_samples(uint32_t samples);
 
+void
+nvk_cmd_disable_tir(struct nvk_cmd_buffer *cmd)
+{
+   const struct nvk_device *dev = nvk_cmd_buffer_device(cmd);
+
+   if (!cmd->state.gfx.tir_maybe_on)
+      return;
+
+   cmd->state.gfx.tir_maybe_on = false;
+
+   /* Only a device with VK_NV_framebuffer_mixed_samples enabled ever turns
+    * it on; the queue's init state has it off.
+    */
+   if (!dev->vk.enabled_extensions.NV_framebuffer_mixed_samples)
+      return;
+
+   struct nv_push *p = nvk_cmd_buffer_push(cmd, 2);
+   P_IMMD(p, NVB197, SET_TIR, MODE_DISABLED);
+}
+
 static void
 nvk_cmd_set_sample_layout(struct nvk_cmd_buffer *cmd,
                           enum nil_sample_layout sample_layout)
@@ -1406,6 +1447,12 @@ nvk_CmdBeginRendering(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer,
 
    nvk_cmd_buffer_dirty_render_pass(cmd);
 
+   /* No target-independent rasterization across the SET_ANTI_ALIAS and the
+    * load-op clears below; the first draw that wants it turns it back on
+    * (nvk_flush_mixed_samples(), rasterization samples are dirty).
+    */
+   nvk_cmd_disable_tir(cmd);
+
    const size_t zcull_count = 47;
    struct nv_push *p = nvk_cmd_buffer_push(
       cmd, NVK_MAX_RTS * 12 + 46 + zcull_count
@@ -3959,6 +4006,107 @@ vk_to_nak_sample_location(VkSampleLocationEXT loc)
    };
 }
 
+static uint32_t
+nvk_raster_samples_mode(uint32_t samples)
+{
+   switch (samples) {
+   case 2:  return NVB197_SET_ANTI_ALIAS_RASTER_SAMPLES_MODE_2X1_D3D;
+   case 4:  return NVB197_SET_ANTI_ALIAS_RASTER_SAMPLES_MODE_2X2;
+   case 8:  return NVB197_SET_ANTI_ALIAS_RASTER_SAMPLES_MODE_4X2_D3D;
+   case 16: return NVB197_SET_ANTI_ALIAS_RASTER_SAMPLES_MODE_4X4;
+   default: return NVB197_SET_ANTI_ALIAS_RASTER_SAMPLES_MODE_1X1;
+   }
+}
+
+static uint32_t
+vk_to_nvb197_tir_modulation(VkCoverageModulationModeNV mode)
+{
+   switch (mode) {
+   case VK_COVERAGE_MODULATION_MODE_RGB_NV:
+      return NVB197_SET_TIR_MODULATION_COMPONENT_SELECT_MODULATE_RGB;
+   case VK_COVERAGE_MODULATION_MODE_ALPHA_NV:
+      return NVB197_SET_TIR_MODULATION_COMPONENT_SELECT_MODULATE_ALPHA_ONLY;
+   case VK_COVERAGE_MODULATION_MODE_RGBA_NV:
+      return NVB197_SET_TIR_MODULATION_COMPONENT_SELECT_MODULATE_RGBA;
+   default:
+      return NVB197_SET_TIR_MODULATION_COMPONENT_SELECT_NO_MODULATION;
+   }
+}
+
+/* VK_NV_framebuffer_mixed_samples: a draw that rasterizes at more samples
+ * than its color attachments have (rasterizationSamples > the attachments'
+ * sample count, which nvk_BeginRendering() programmed with SET_ANTI_ALIAS)
+ * turns on target-independent rasterization: SET_ANTI_ALIAS_RASTER gives
+ * the raster sample count, the pixel shader's coverage input (covmask) has
+ * one bit per raster sample, and color writes see the coverage reduced to
+ * the color samples.  D3D11.1 target-independent rasterization (Direct2D's
+ * anti-aliased fills: ForcedSampleCount 16 with a single-sample render
+ * target) is exactly this.
+ *
+ * The extension requires sampleShadingEnable = VK_FALSE in that case and
+ * a depth/stencil attachment to have rasterizationSamples samples if any
+ * depth or stencil test is on, so the per-pass sample masks (the MME's
+ * SET_ANTI_ALIAS state, from the attachments' count) and the depth/stencil
+ * layout need nothing new.
+ */
+static void
+nvk_flush_mixed_samples(struct nvk_cmd_buffer *cmd)
+{
+   const struct nvk_rendering_state *render = &cmd->state.gfx.render;
+   const struct vk_dynamic_graphics_state *dyn =
+      &cmd->vk.dynamic_graphics_state;
+
+   const uint32_t raster_samples = dyn->ms.rasterization_samples;
+   const bool mixed = render->samples != 0 &&
+                      raster_samples > render->samples;
+
+   if (!mixed) {
+      nvk_cmd_disable_tir(cmd);
+      return;
+   }
+
+   struct nv_push *p = nvk_cmd_buffer_push(cmd, 10);
+
+   P_IMMD(p, NVB197, SET_ANTI_ALIAS_RASTER,
+          nvk_raster_samples_mode(raster_samples));
+
+   const uint32_t modulation =
+      vk_to_nvb197_tir_modulation(dyn->ms.coverage_modulation_mode);
+   P_IMMD(p, NVB197, SET_TIR_MODULATION, modulation);
+
+   if (modulation != NVB197_SET_TIR_MODULATION_COMPONENT_SELECT_NO_MODULATION) {
+      const bool table = dyn->ms.coverage_modulation_table_enable;
+      P_IMMD(p, NVB197, SET_TIR_MODULATION_FUNCTION,
+             table ? SELECT_TABLE : SELECT_LINEAR);
+
+      if (table) {
+         /* pCoverageModulationTable[i] is the factor for a color sample
+          * with i + 1 of its associated raster samples covered; the
+          * hardware takes 16 unorm8 coefficients in the same order.
+          */
+         uint8_t coef[16] = { 0 };
+         const uint32_t count = MIN2(dyn->ms.coverage_modulation_table_count,
+                                     ARRAY_SIZE(coef));
+         for (uint32_t i = 0; i < count; i++) {
+            coef[i] = float_to_ubyte(dyn->ms.coverage_modulation_table[i]);
+         }
+
+         P_MTHD(p, NVB197, SET_TIR_MODULATION_COEFFICIENT_TABLE(0));
+         for (uint32_t i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
+            P_NVB197_SET_TIR_MODULATION_COEFFICIENT_TABLE(p, i, {
+               .v0 = coef[i * 4 + 0],
+               .v1 = coef[i * 4 + 1],
+               .v2 = coef[i * 4 + 2],
+               .v3 = coef[i * 4 + 3],
+            });
+         }
+      }
+   }
+
+   P_IMMD(p, NVB197, SET_TIR, MODE_RASTER_N_TARGET_M);
+   cmd->state.gfx.tir_maybe_on = true;
+}
+
 static void
 nvk_flush_ms_state(struct nvk_cmd_buffer *cmd)
 {
@@ -3980,13 +4128,23 @@ nvk_flush_ms_state(struct nvk_cmd_buffer *cmd)
          nvk_cmd_set_sample_layout(cmd, nil_choose_sample_layout(samples));
       } else {
          /* Multisample information MAY be missing (rasterizationSamples == 0)
-          * if rasterizer discard is enabled.
+          * if rasterizer discard is enabled.  With
+          * VK_NV_framebuffer_mixed_samples it may be more than the
+          * attachments' sample count (nvk_flush_mixed_samples()).
           */
          assert(dyn->ms.rasterization_samples == 0 ||
-                dyn->ms.rasterization_samples == render->samples);
+                dyn->ms.rasterization_samples >= render->samples);
       }
    }
 
+   if (nvk_cmd_buffer_device(cmd)->vk.enabled_extensions.NV_framebuffer_mixed_samples &&
+       (BITSET_TEST(dyn->dirty, MESA_VK_DYNAMIC_MS_RASTERIZATION_SAMPLES) ||
+        BITSET_TEST(dyn->dirty, MESA_VK_DYNAMIC_MS_COVERAGE_MODULATION_MODE) ||
+        BITSET_TEST(dyn->dirty,
+                    MESA_VK_DYNAMIC_MS_COVERAGE_MODULATION_TABLE_ENABLE) ||
+        BITSET_TEST(dyn->dirty, MESA_VK_DYNAMIC_MS_COVERAGE_MODULATION_TABLE)))
+      nvk_flush_mixed_samples(cmd);
+
    if (BITSET_TEST(dyn->dirty, MESA_VK_DYNAMIC_MS_ALPHA_TO_COVERAGE_ENABLE) ||
        BITSET_TEST(dyn->dirty, MESA_VK_DYNAMIC_MS_ALPHA_TO_ONE_ENABLE)) {
       struct nv_push *p = nvk_cmd_buffer_push(cmd, 2);
@@ -4007,8 +4165,14 @@ nvk_flush_ms_state(struct nvk_cmd_buffer *cmd)
          sl = vk_standard_sample_locations_state(samples);
       }
 
-      struct nak_sample_location push_sl[NVK_MAX_SAMPLES];
-      for (uint32_t i = 0; i < sl->per_pixel; i++)
+      /* The shader-visible positions (gl_SamplePosition, interpolation at a
+       * sample index) hold NVK_MAX_SAMPLES; a 16-sample mixed-samples raster
+       * (more than any attachment can have) only programs the hardware's
+       * positions below.  Sample shading, the use of the rest, is not
+       * allowed there.
+       */
+      struct nak_sample_location push_sl[NVK_MAX_SAMPLES] = { 0 };
+      for (uint32_t i = 0; i < MIN2(sl->per_pixel, NVK_MAX_SAMPLES); i++)
          push_sl[i] = vk_to_nak_sample_location(sl->locations[i]);
 
       nvk_descriptor_state_set_root_array(cmd, &cmd->state.gfx.descriptors,
diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
index 615fd601..ae735fac 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_physical_device.c
@@ -346,6 +346,7 @@ nvk_get_device_extensions(const struct nvk_instance *instance,
       .GOOGLE_user_type = true,
       .MESA_image_alignment_control = true,
       .NV_compute_shader_derivatives = info->cls_eng3d >= TURING_A,
+      .NV_framebuffer_mixed_samples = info->cls_eng3d >= MAXWELL_B,
       .NV_shader_atomic_float16_vector = info->cls_eng3d >= TURING_A,
       .NV_shader_sm_builtins = true,
       .NVX_image_view_handle = info->cls_eng3d >= MAXWELL_A, /* needs true bindless descriptors */
@@ -704,9 +705,9 @@ nvk_get_device_features(const struct nv_device_info *info,
       .extendedDynamicState3ViewportSwizzle = false,
       .extendedDynamicState3CoverageToColorEnable = false,
       .extendedDynamicState3CoverageToColorLocation = false,
-      .extendedDynamicState3CoverageModulationMode = false,
-      .extendedDynamicState3CoverageModulationTableEnable = false,
-      .extendedDynamicState3CoverageModulationTable = false,
+      .extendedDynamicState3CoverageModulationMode = info->cls_eng3d >= MAXWELL_B,
+      .extendedDynamicState3CoverageModulationTableEnable = info->cls_eng3d >= MAXWELL_B,
+      .extendedDynamicState3CoverageModulationTable = info->cls_eng3d >= MAXWELL_B,
       .extendedDynamicState3CoverageReductionMode = false,
       .extendedDynamicState3RepresentativeFragmentTestEnable = false,
       .extendedDynamicState3ShadingRateImageEnable = false,
